{
  "about": "The customer deploy preflight (scripts/deploy.sh) runs validate:customer:chain, the members of validate:chain, validate and lint:chain marked keep here. Every other member keeps running in npm run validate, npm run lint and CI; each is named here with the category whose one-line reason says why a customer deploy leaves it out. test/validate-customer-preflight.ts fails when those chains and this file disagree.",
  "commonReason": "Every left-out member grades code that CI graded on the same commit. On a customer machine the preflight establishes that this tree is that commit's code with its locked dependencies (lint:deps-installed), that it builds and typechecks, and it re-runs the gates for the key material the browser handles and the page that holds it.",
  "keepReason": "Guards the customer's keys in the browser: key generation, capsule and envelope opening, splitting and reassembly, the in-console break-glass restore and prune, the recovery sheet, the committed bundle, and the Worker's security headers and CSP that protect the page holding the key.",
  "dropReasons": {
    "cross-repo": "Reads a sibling checkout (engine, docs, or other internal checkouts) or refuses when one is behind its own origin/main; a customer checkout sits on a release tag with no siblings beside it, so here it can only refuse or skip.",
    "dev-process": "Grades how this repository is developed (gate wiring, lint policy, coverage drivers, CI, ledgers), not the console this deploy uploads.",
    "copy": "Grades wording, claims and presentation against the code; it protects what a reader is told, not the key material the browser handles.",
    "console-screens": "Grades a console screen, component or flow that does not generate, open, split or hold key material and does not set the page's security headers."
  },
  "lintChainRule": "Every member of lint:chain not marked keep here is left out. lint:deps-installed runs as its own preflight step before the chain. The rest grade code shape, copy, the development process or sibling checkouts, not the key material the browser handles, and they keep running in npm run lint and CI.",
  "measured": {
    "seconds": 75,
    "text": "It took 36 to 75 seconds when measured, at load averages from 15 to 110."
  },
